{"id":"n-20261020-w2fuhp","category":"health","display_title":"Breaking the Silence on Lichen Sclerosus","display_title_he":"שבירת השתיקה לגבי ליכן סקלרוזוס","short_summary":"Two women share their long struggles with misdiagnoses and a little-known gynaecological condition called lichen sclerosus.","english_level":"C1","words":465,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"BBC News","domain":"bbc.co.uk","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9vgr43l7pdpo","title":"I have a condition people are too embarrassed to talk about","published_at":"2026-10-19T23:11:13.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-19T23:11:13.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-20T06:29:15.001Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Navigating the medical system with a misunderstood condition can be an isolating and harrowing experience, particularly when social taboos discourage open conversations about gynaecological health. For years, patients suffering from intimate discomfort have found their symptoms dismissed, misattributed, or entirely overlooked by healthcare professionals. This widespread lack of awareness often leads to prolonged suffering, profound mental health struggles, and devastating physical consequences.","Monica Thomas was just a teenager when she first experienced persistent intimate itching and soreness. Despite seeking medical help numerous times, practitioners repeatedly dismissed her symptoms as thrush. Over a period of just six months, she underwent twenty-eight examinations before finally being offered a biopsy. Her condition eventually deteriorated to the point where she was bedbound because walking became excruciating. Doctors erroneously provided medication for herpes and even suggested testing for human immunodeficiency virus, repeatedly telling her she was far too young for the actual underlying issue. Eventually, she received a diagnosis of lichen sclerosus at thirty-four years of age, yet she still navigates her ongoing management entirely on her own without routine medical check-ups.","Similarly, Clare Baumhaeur endured symptoms from the tender age of five, suffering through tears, blisters, and sores well into her adult life without realizing her anatomy was atypical. Despite undergoing multiple smear tests over the decades, healthcare providers never raised concerns. When she was forty-three, a general practitioner mistakenly diagnosed her with herpes and instructed her to visit a sexual health clinic, an alarming proposition after twenty-five years of marriage. A subsequent biopsy revealed not only lichen sclerosus but also vulval cancer, a condition she had never encountered before in a part of the body no medical professional had ever mentioned to her.","According to medical specialists, lichen sclerosus is a lifelong inflammatory condition affecting the genital region. It produces white patches, severe soreness, splitting, and tearing of the skin, and while it affects both men and women, it is predominantly diagnosed in women over the age of fifty. The exact origin remains unknown, though experts theorize that the immune system might mistakenly attack healthy skin tissue, and physical friction can trigger or aggravate the symptoms. Although it can cause pain during sexual intercourse and urination, specialists emphasize that the condition is entirely non-contagious and distinct from sexually transmitted infections.","University research estimating that the condition affects roughly one percent of women is widely considered an underestimate. Diagnostic delays can span decades, and many individuals ultimately go their entire lives without knowing what is wrong. Experts emphasize that urgent research into true prevalence rates is necessary, alongside better education for healthcare professionals to overcome the embarrassment and shame preventing patients from seeking timely assistance. Advocates urge anyone experiencing persistent bodily changes to document their symptoms carefully, seek multiple opinions, and refuse to accept dismissal when searching for answers."],"facts":[{"fact":"Monica Thomas and Clare Baumhaeur faced decades of misdiagnoses before discovering they had lichen sclerosus, a chronic inflammatory condition affecting the genitals.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Lichen sclerosus causes severe itching, soreness, white patches, and tears, carrying a small risk of vulval cancer if left untreated or unmanaged.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Research estimated the condition affects roughly 1% of women, though experts believe this figure is an underestimate due to widespread diagnostic delays and social taboos.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Navigating","lemma":"navigate","pos":"verb","he":"התנהלות / ניווט","name":false},{"text":"medical system","lemma":"medical system","pos":"compound","name":false,"he":"מערכת הרפואה"},{"text":"misunderstood","lemma":"misunderstood","pos":"adjective","he":"לא מובן נכון","name":false},{"text":"condition","lemma":"condition","pos":"noun","he":"מצב רפואי","name":false},{"text":"isolating","lemma":"isolating","pos":"adjective","he":"מבודד","name":false},{"text":"harrowing","lemma":"harrowing","pos":"adjective","he":"מטלטל / קשה","name":false},{"text":"experience","lemma":"experience","pos":"noun","he":"חוויה","name":false},{"text":"social","lemma":"social","pos":"adjective","he":"חברתי","name":false},{"text":"taboos","lemma":"taboo","pos":"noun","he":"טאבו","name":false},{"text":"discourage","lemma":"discourage","pos":"verb","he":"ממריץ נגד / מרתיע","name":false},{"text":"open","lemma":"open","pos":"adjective","he":"פתוח","name":false},{"text":"conversations","lemma":"conversation","pos":"noun","he":"שיחות","name":false},{"text":"gynaecological","lemma":"gynaecological","pos":"adjective","he":"גינקולוגי","name":false},{"text":"health","lemma":"health","pos":"noun","he":"בריאות","name":false},{"text":"suffering","lemma":"suffering","pos":"noun","he":"סבל","name":